+## 10. Reconstruction 2026-09-14
+
+`mul_mat_vec_q5_k.comp` was lost to an HQ `git checkout --` during the planted-red cycle. The C++
+and test changes survived uncommitted. This section records the rebuild.
+
+### What was rebuilt
+
+Only `mul_mat_vec_q5_k.comp`, reconstructed to §2 / §4 / §6 with no change of design:
+
+| Piece | Form |
+|---|---|
+| `layout (constant_id = 3) const uint ARIFI_Q5K_B_HOIST = 1;` | Declared default 1, matching the Q6_K precedent. All three surviving registrations pass an explicit 4th element, so the declared default only binds a caller that passes three. |
+| `decode_superblock(...)` | Verbatim lift of the shipped per-row decode. No expression rewritten; the eight `sc*` and sixteen `q4_*` locals became `out FLOAT_TYPE sc[8]` / `out FLOAT_TYPE q4[16]`. |
+| `load_activations(...)` | `out vec2 by[8]` = the shipped `by10, by116, by132, by148, by20, by216, by232, by248`, in that order. |
+| `accumulate_column(...)` | Verbatim lift of the shipped inner body, `inout FLOAT_TYPE t`. `sc[0],sc[1],sc[4],sc[5]` carry the main term and `sc[2],sc[3],sc[6],sc[7]` the `smin` term, as shipped. |
+| `calc_superblock()` arm 1 | `dmv[NUM_ROWS]`, `scv[NUM_ROWS][8]`, `q4v[NUM_ROWS][16]`; decode all rows, then `for j { load_activations once; for n { accumulate_column } }`. |
+| `calc_superblock()` arm 0 | Single-row `dm` / `sc[8]` / `q4[16]` scoped inside the `n` loop, activations reloaded per row — the shipped order. Deliberately NOT sharing arm 1's `[NUM_ROWS]` storage, so arm 0 does not carry the hoist's register pressure and the pairing measures the real difference. |
+
+§6 coverage limit 1 (whether glslang accepts a row of a spec-constant-sized 2-D array as an array
+argument) is now **CLOSED by compilation** — `scv[n]` and `q4v[n]` were accepted as-is; the fallback
+of passing whole arrays plus an index was not needed. Limits 2 (spill), 3 (unroll/scratch), 4
+(`f16_f32` and `_id`) and 5 (no model) remain open. **Register and scratch figures were NOT obtained**:
+`RADV_DEBUG=shaderstats` runs through `perf`, and perf was out of scope for this session.
+
+### Build
+
+`ninja -C build-vulkan test-backend-ops`, `rc=0`, receipt `r48-evidence/39-build.txt` + `.rc`. The
+step list is the independent proof the new shader is in the binary rather than a stale SPIR-V blob —
+the arms are bit-identical, so a green/green correctness pair on its own would not have
+distinguished the two:
+
+```
+[5/9] Generate vulkan shaders for mul_mat_vec_q5_k.comp
+[6/9] Building CXX object ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/CMakeFiles/ggml-vulkan.dir/mul_mat_vec_q5_k.comp.cpp.obj
+```
+
+### sha256 of the three changed files, as committed
+
+```
+5d2457bbc5a07c3d2414852864ad3c88100b5b062a9b3ca1e3f02082646b0992  ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
+e578ba23c3b0b3fe2e9322116a87425adeac9206d22dbecb3e762e026da41946  ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vec_q5_k.comp
+4f097859d525b0d443adfd4249ecdcca383a278122d6f48a081cd3d35354df3e  tests/test-backend-ops.cpp
+```
+
+### Correctness receipts
+
+Command in both arms: `build-vulkan/bin/test-backend-ops.exe test -o MUL_MAT -b Vulkan0 -p "type_a=q5_K"`.
+
+| Arm | Env | Receipt | rc | Q5_K cases | FAIL |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Hoisted (default) | unset | `r48-evidence/40-mulmat-q5k-hoist-on.txt` + `.rc` | 0 | 61 | 0 |
+| Shipped order | `GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_B_HOIST=0` | `r48-evidence/41-mulmat-q5k-hoist-off.txt` + `.rc` | 0 | 61 | 0 |
+| Hoisted, `n=1` forced onto f32 | `GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_MMVQ_N1=0` | `r48-evidence/42-mulmat-q5k-hoist-on-n1f32.txt` + `.rc` | 0 | 61 | 0 |
+
+Each run carries its own device-init receipt line — `q5_k mat-vec activation-hoist: ON` in 40, `OFF`
+in 41 — so the two files are proof the env override reached the pipeline, not just that the binary
+ran twice. All three ended `2/2 backends passed`.
+
+**§6 limit 6 is CLOSED.** The 61 rows are not the pre-existing set: the receipt contains
+`m = {7, 16, 1023, 4096, 5120, 17407, 17408, 248320}`, so the new 27B shapes and both row-tail rows
+(`m = 17407`, `m = 7`) actually executed rather than being silently skipped.
+
+**Receipt 42 exists because 40 and 41 do not exercise `NUM_COLS = 1` of this shader.** Under default
+routing Q5_K `n = 1` goes to MMVQ, so those two arms only test the reconstruction at `n = 2..8`.
+`GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_MMVQ_N1=0` puts `n = 1` on the f32 shader, which is the only numerical check of the
+hoisted arm at `NUM_COLS = 1` — the width the `_id` registration at `:7246` hard-codes. The `_id`
+pipeline itself is still only proven to *create* (its device-init receipt prints), not to compute;
+§6 limit 4 stands.
+
+**No perf run, no `llama-*` run, no model was loaded.** The §7 pairing is still owed to HQ.
+
+### Commit
+
+`8728c86d6dd1c9809ae27663778d124a15b690e9` on `lane-234/r48-matvec-kernels-2026-09-14`, parent
+`9ff4644b1`. It carries `ggml-vulkan.cpp`, `mul_mat_vec_q5_k.comp`, `test-backend-ops.cpp` and the
+three markdown files. `r48-evidence/` is deliberately **not** in it.
+
+This section was written after that commit — a commit cannot contain its own SHA — so the report is
+dirty in the working tree against `8728c86`. HQ owns whether §10 lands as a follow-up commit.
